new={"quantity":"Q57: how much of the N/S HCN/HCO+ contrast (1.45 at 1-0, 1.50 at 3-2, 2.2\" beam) excitation, density, temperature and opacity differences can produce vs an abundance ratio change (joint N+S non-LTE bracket; round 2 with physical priors, profile likelihood, error-model sensitivity)",
"target":"N and S, 2.2\" beam, 1-0 and 3-2 (+13C 1-0)",
"value":"(1) Physical priors do not change the answer. Forcing log n>=3.8-4.2 (the earlier best fits sat at the grid edge log n=3, N(HCO+)=2e16, i.e. L=0.6-6 kpc for x=1e-8-1e-9) and L<=100-450 pc: Delta(-2lnL) vs Hfull Hexc 7.7-7.8, Hcol 6.7-7.4, Habun 3.3-3.8 (X 40-100); BF vs Hfull Hexc 1.5-1.8, Hcol 0.28-0.40, Habun 61-68; A_N/A_S median 1.58, 16-84% 1.26-2.0, P(>1)=0.93-0.94, P(>1.3)=0.74-0.77 (5% quantile drops from 1.26 to 1.0). The best N fit moves to Tk 73-237 K, n 6e3-1.6e4, N(HCO+) 1-8e15 (eta~0.1): the Q34/Q44-like regime (n~1e4); S Tk 150-300 K, n 1.6e4, N(HCO+) 1e15. The L constraint is non-binding once n>=6e3 (L~30-50 pc for x=1e-8). (2) Profile likelihood of the model 1-0 contrast with equal A (excitation+opacity only), delta(-2lnL) relative to each hypothesis' own best: Hexc best 1.10, within dchi2<=1: 1.00-1.20, <=4: 0.95-1.26 (X 40-100) [1.00-1.32 / 0.91-1.51 for X 20-200]; Hcol best 1.10-1.15, dchi2<=1: 0.95-1.26, <=4: 0.8-1.38. Observed 1.45: Hexc/Hcol are 7.7/5.0 (unconstrained) or 7.7/6.7 (n>=3.8) above Hfull, i.e. p=0.05 (1.9 sigma, 3 dof) and p=0.08-0.035 (1.7-2.1 sigma, 2 dof); 12.7-15.4 (2.8-3.2 sigma) if the systematic errors are halved, 3.5 (p=0.3, 1 sigma) if doubled. So 'excitation/opacity alone cannot reach 1.45' is a ~2 sigma statement (range 1-3 sigma over the error model), not 2.5-3. Best-fit contrasts with equal A: 1.09-1.13 (1-0), 1.23-1.35 (3-2) vs 1.45/1.50, i.e. 20-45% (1-0) and 50-70% (3-2) of ln(contrast). (3) Occam: pure abundance (Habun: same Tk,n,N(HCO+),X at N and S; only N(HCN)/N(HCO+) differs) is preferred to Hexc by BF 41 (unconstrained), 35-44 (physical), 25 (flat log n 3-6), 16-27 (X 20-200); to Hcol by 55-250. Error model: halved errors BF(Habun/Hexc) 370-2200; doubled errors 2.6-7. It never falls below 2.6 in 42 prior x error-model combinations, but its size depends mostly on the error model and the 12C/13C prior; it is evidence that N and S can share one gas state (Tk,n,N) and differ only in [HCN]/[HCO+], NOT a proof that excitation differences are excluded (Hexc has BF 0.03-4 relative to Hfull in the same grid). The pure-excitation/abundance models are not nested: Habun has 6 free parameters vs 7 for Hexc and fits better (dchi2 3.3-3.8 vs 7.7). (4) Physical consequences: N(HCN)/N(HCO+) = 3.2 [2.5-4.0] at N and 2.0 [1.6-2.5] at S (A_N/A_S ~1.6 [1.26-2.0]); for [HCO+]/[H2]=1e-9-1e-8 this is x(HCN)=(3-4)e-9-(3-4)e-8 at N vs (2)e-9-2e-8 at S, a ~60% HCN enhancement at N (vs ~x1.0 at S) with HCO+ unchanged. Alternative branch (X_S >= 130 vs X_N~80, free per-nucleus 12C/13C, HcolX): contrast 1.18-1.31 (1-0) / 1.32-1.44 (3-2), Delta chi2 1.2-3.2 and BF 0.6-1.4 against Hfull, i.e. not excluded. Discriminating predictions: observed H13CO+/HCO+ = 0.027+-0.004 (N), 0.015+-0.004 (S), N/S 1.8+-0.6; under shared X (abundance branch) thin 13C/12C line ratios of ANY species (HN13C/HNC, 13CO/C18O, H13CO+/HCO+) should be equal at N and S (N/S ~1, only the moderate N opacity tau(HCO+)~1.3 raises 12C-based ratios) and the HCN-family ratios H13CN/H13CO+ should show N/S = A_N/A_S ~1.6 (observed 3.7+-5.5, uninformative); under the 12C/13C branch every 13C/12C ratio (HN13C/HNC, 13CO/C18O, H13CO+/HCO+) at S is lower than at N by X_S/X_N ~1.6-2 (and H13CN/H13CO+ N/S ~1). A single deep HN13C/H13CN or 13CO/C18O pair at N and S in matched beams would decide; a deeper H13CN at S (need sigma <0.1 K km/s vs 0.35 now) would too.",
"unit":"ratios / delta(-2lnL) / BF","uncertainty":"A_N/A_S quantised on 0.1 dex (1.26/1.58/2.0/2.5). Significance: 1.7-2.1 sigma for Hexc/Hcol vs Hfull at default errors; the systematic-error scale moves it from 1 to 3 sigma. BFs depend on prior volume (X 40-100 vs 20-200 lowers Habun/Hexc from 41 to 26) and error model. One-zone, equal filling of HCN, HCO+ and 13C lines, thin 13C. S H13CN (0.24+-0.35 vs 0.7-0.9 predicted) is a ~1.5 sigma tension in every model and X_S~100 hits the prior edge. Grid has no n<1e3 or two-component (core+envelope) model; the 2.2\" one-zone fit of an ~100 pc HCN-rich core at N is an average; 4-3 and HNC not used; Tk not independently fixed.",
"confidence":"low","evidence":"scripts/s353_q57_joint_bracket.py (env Q57_SYS/Q57_MOD), s354_q57_bestfits.py, s356_q57_physical.py, s357_update_report_q57r2.py (out/q57/s356_s*_m*.txt, s353_*.txt, s354_*.txt); inputs Q44 s261, Q29/Q34/Q59 data vector; Q56 s346; lit: Tang+19 A&A 629 A6 (12C/13C), Harada+18 ApJ 855 49 (nuclear HCN/HCO+ at 1.7\")","assumptions":A}
